~~ Public | Today’s AI is often judged with tests that are easy to score but do not always show how well it works in real life. We argue that language-based games can be a better way to study AI, because they test how well a system understands people, goals, and changing conversations. We describe examples like Diplomacy and Dungeons & Dragons and explain why these games can reveal strengths and weaknesses that standard tests miss.